.TH QIMAGE 1 "September 2026" "Qore ImageMagick module" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qimage \- inspect, convert and transform images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qimage
.I command
.RI [ input ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qimage
uses ImageMagick 7 through Qore to inspect image information, resize and
convert images, apply effects, draw text and shapes, and manage profiles.
Transform commands require an output path or an explicit in-place option.
Existing output paths can be replaced. Formats and delegates are subject
to the distribution ImageMagick security policy.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B fonts, formats
List fonts or supported image formats.
.TP
.B info, identify, props, profile, pixel
Inspect images, properties, profiles and pixels. See command-specific help
for property, profile and pixel modification options.
.TP
.B convert, resize, crop, rotate
Change image format, dimensions or geometry.
.TP
.B adjust, blur, sharpen, effect, noise
Adjust colors and apply filters or effects; --method selects an operation.
.TP
.B composite, annotate, draw, border, strip
Combine images, draw text/shapes, add borders or remove metadata.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show general or command-specific help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Display version.
.TP
.BR -o ", " --output " " path
Write output to path.
.TP
.BR -i ", " --in-place
Modify the input file directly.
.TP
.BR -F ", " --format " " format
Select the output format; otherwise it is inferred from the output suffix.
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quality " " number
Set output compression quality.
.TP
.BR -m ", " --method " " name
Select the transformation method.
.TP
.B --width, --height
Set target dimensions for relevant commands.
.TP
.BR -C ", " --no-color
Disable terminal colors.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
Increase verbosity.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
qimage info photo.png
qimage resize photo.png --width 400 --height 300 -o thumbnail.png
qimage convert photo.png -F JPEG -q 90 -o photo.jpg
qimage annotate photo.png --text 'Hello' --font DejaVu-Sans --font-size 18 -o label.png
qimage resize thumbnail.png --width 200 --height 150 --in-place
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore (1)
.br
Use qimage COMMAND --help for command-specific arguments and methods.
